@startuml seq_test_attempt
!include diagram-style.puml
hide footbox
title Aptitude attempt — intended lifecycle and recovery
caption Service/worker design; current repository implements models, not these endpoints.
actor Student
boundary "React test screen" as C
control "Authorized API / AttemptService" as AS
database "MongoDB" as DB
control "Server timeout coordinator\n(planned)" as TIMER

== Start or resume (TST-3 / SAFE-1) ==
Student -> C : open test
C -> AS : POST /api/tests/{id}/attempts
AS -> AS : authenticate student + verify test availability
AS -> DB : find by studentId + testId
alt existing SUBMITTED attempt
  AS --> C : 409 ATTEMPT_EXISTS
else existing IN_PROGRESS attempt
  AS -> AS : check original deadline; finalize if due
  AS --> C : existing attempt or closed/result response
else no attempt
  AS -> DB : load test + private question keys
  AS -> DB : create unique Attempt with snapshots\nstartedAt = server now; endsAt = start + duration
  note right of DB
    Concurrent duplicate-key creation:
    reload/resume the existing attempt.
  end note
  AS --> C : 201 public questions + answers + endsAt
end

== Select / acknowledge / recover (TST-4 / SAFE-1) ==
loop each answer selection while permitted
  C -> AS : PATCH /api/attempts/{id}/answers\n{questionId, optionIdx}
  AS -> AS : verify owner, status, snapshot option\nand agreed deadline/grace policy
  AS -> DB : persist validated answer + lastSavedAt\nconflict-safe write, not stale whole-map replacement
  DB --> AS : acknowledged
  AS --> C : 204; UI may now show Saved
end
opt browser refresh / reconnect
  C -> AS : start/resume same test
  AS -> DB : load existing state
  AS --> C : saved answers + original endsAt\n(or closed state if already finalized)
end

== Finalize once (TST-5 / TST-6) ==
alt manual submit
  C -> AS : POST /api/attempts/{id}/submit
else deadline reached without client
  TIMER -> AS : finalize overdue active attempt
end
AS -> AS : score saved answers using snapshot keys
AS -> DB : atomically close attempt + create canonical Result\nusing agreed transaction/recovery strategy
DB --> AS : durable state / existing result on retry
AS --> C : manual request returns score + topicBreakdown
note over AS, TIMER
  No dependency on a browser remaining open.
  TST-5 rejects answers after endsAt +30 seconds;
  handling of the intermediate grace window needs team agreement.
  A submitted attempt is never silently reopened.
end note
note over AS, DB
  Result holds score and topicBreakdown, not duplicated Attempt.score.
  Analytics reads Results; a read-only Python engine does not write snapshots.
end note
@enduml
